      "index": 0,
      "text": "85, 1566 + 13920 + 69600 = 85, 1566 + 13920 is 15486, plus 69600 is 85,086.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 174 and 489?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 489 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 174 by 9 (the ones place digit of 489):\n   \\[\n   174 \\times 9 = 1566\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 174 by 80 (the tens place digit of 489):\n   \\[\n   174 \\times 80 = 13920\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 174 by 400 (the hundreds place digit of 489):\n   \\[\n   174 \\times 400 = 69600\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1566 + 13920 + 69600 = 85186\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{85186}.",
