      "text": "145,755.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 255 and 573?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 573 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 255 by 3 (the ones place digit of 573):\n   \\[\n   255 \\times 3 = 765\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 255 by 70 (the tens place digit of 573):\n   \\[\n   255 \\times 70 = 17,850\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 255 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 573):\n   \\[\n   255 \\times 500 = 127,500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n765 + 17,850 + 127,500 = 145,755\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{145,\\!755}\\).",
