      "text": "904200.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 928 and 975?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 975 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 928 by 5 (the ones place digit of 975):\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 5 = 4640\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 928 by 70 (the tens place digit of 975):\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 70 = 64960\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 928 by 900 (the hundreds place digit of 975):\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 900 = 835200\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n4640 + 64960 + 835200 = 904800\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{904800}\\).",
