      "text": "135 \u00d7 591 = 79,785.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 135 and 591?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 591 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 135 by 1 (the ones place digit of 591):\n   \\[\n   135 \\times 1 = 135\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 135 by 90 (the tens place digit of 591):\n   \\[\n   135 \\times 90 = 12,150\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 135 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 591):\n   \\[\n   135 \\times 500 = 67,500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n135 + 12,150 + 67,500 = 79,785\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{79,\\!785}\\).",
